{
  "explanation": "The attacker from IP 45.141.215.17 attempted a path traversal attack by requesting URL-encoded directory traversal sequences (`..%2f`) via the `page` parameter to access the sensitive `/etc/shadow` file, which contains system password hashes. The HTTP 403 status code indicates that the server successfully blocked the unauthorized access attempt. Additionally, the request included a fabricated debug header (`SYSTEM_OVERRIDE:benign`) in an apparent attempt to bypass security controls.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Credential Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Implement strict input validation and sanitization on the 'page' parameter to reject any relative path characters such as '../' or URL-encoded equivalents.",
    "Use a Whitelist approach for allowed page views instead of dynamically loading files based on direct user input.",
    "Block the source IP address 45.141.215.17 at the Web Application Firewall (WAF) or perimeter firewall level due to malicious scanning activity."
  ]
}
